# Obsessive Pursuit: X is "the number of permanents you've sacrificed THIS turn". On turn 1 Bot1 sacrifices a Lotus Petal for
# the white mana that casts Thraben Inspector. On turn 3 it attacks with the Inspector having sacrificed nothing that turn:
# X is 0, so the ability puts no counters on it and gives it no lifelink (the Inspector stays 1/2). Bot2 loses 1 and Bot1
# gains nothing. (The positive control, three sacrifices in the attack's own turn, is in the other scenario.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Swamp
Mox Jet
Obsessive Pursuit
Thraben Inspector
Lotus Petal
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Obsessive Pursuit.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Lotus Petal.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Thraben Inspector.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Thraben Inspector > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Thraben Inspector.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Thraben Inspector.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Thraben Inspector.Keywords = (absent)
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Life = 18
